The relevant date for establishing the Commission's jurisdiction over a concentration is whichever of the following dates is earlier:
1. The date of the conclusion of the binding legal agreement;
2. The announcement of a public bid;
3. The acquisition of a controlling interest; or
4. The date of the first notification (including notifications based on a good faith intention to conclude an agreement or an announced intention to make a public bid) [CJN para. 155, 156].
